    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Opening brief — brief the topic before you touch anything",
      "prov:value": "Split out of `todo-manager.md` on 2026-09-19 (bean `tdmg`), which had reached\n396 lines against `skill-not-a-document`'s 400-line threshold while carrying\nthree separable disciplines. This is the one that governs what you say\n**before** the work; [`turn-reporting.md`](turn-reporting.md) governs what you\nsay during and after it; [`todo-manager.md`](../../../work-plan/skills/work-plan/todo-manager.md) keeps the bean\nmechanics. Nothing in this file changed in the split.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean tdmg",
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The four parts",
      "prov:value": "**The second row was added 2026-09-23, because \"measured this session\" had\nbeen reading as the safe case. That session ran `grep -c \"@context\"` over a writer, got `0` — correctly, on a\nbranch cut before the commit that added one — then branched from fresh `main`,\ncarried the `0` across without re-running it, briefed on it as current, and\nput a settled question back to the owner as new. Its next commit would have\nreverted merged work.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Before you offer options, check whether it is already ruled (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "1. **The proposals — the design corpus.** They live in the `docs/` of the\n   instance whose stub needs them; today that is\n   [`cat-harness/docs/proposals/`](../../../docs/proposals/index.md), and its\n   `index.md` is where to start.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "docs/proposals/index.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Before you offer options, check whether it is already ruled (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "They were in `fsh-guts/proposals/` until 2026-09-23, under a kind named for\n   *deprecated and throwaway* content, and the owner moved them rather than\n   re-describing the kind: *\"proposals not in fsh-guts but docs/ for needed\n   &lt;stub&gt;\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Before you offer options, check whether it is already ruled (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Added 2026-09-23, when a ruling landed as CODE two hours before a session\n   proposed re-deciding it. It was in none of the three places above: no\n   proposal described it, the bean recording it was already `completed` and so\n   absent from any listing of open work, and the owning skill still described\n   the defect as unfixed. **A decision that shipped is invisible to every\n   instrument that looks for pending ones** — and it is the likeliest kind to\n   have shipped recently, which is exactly when you are most confident your\n   own reading is current.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The failure this is written from",
      "prov:value": "2026-09-22, bean `5kn6`. A session found that `needs` and `dependencies` were\ntwo unreconciled relations, wrote up **three candidate shapes** and declined to\nchoose — citing `AGENTS.md`'s warning that *\"merging the two compositions gives\na closure too broad to fail an audit\"* as the reason.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 5kn6",
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "The failure this is written from",
      "prov:value": "Both halves were wrong. The question was **already settled**:\n`cat-harness/docs/proposals/instance-versioning.md` §3.3 and an owner ruling of\n2026-09-20 — *\"sha is for staging, regernecing in published SEMVER\"* — had\ndecided it, with the gate already implemented. And the citation was about\n**Roles** — `inherits` versus the scoped subprocess stack — not about\ndependencies at all.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "docs/proposals/instance-versioning.md"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Briefing a sibling or a subagent — pass `interaction-modality` on (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Added 2026-11-05 (bean `55ka`), after siblings spawned from coordinating\nsessions (`session_01VQDpPffYARDQ8juksAZScf` on `k3vv` and\n`session_01VQDpPfGantMCt7AV4LCCK2` on `drnh`) asked the owner questions in\nprose without `AskUserQuestion` cards across nine sessions (`drnh`, `rpc6`,\n`f1nc`, `exrp`, `2lfx`, `70hd`, `xxow`, `akiq`/`ay33`/`hd58`, `asq1`). Owner,\n2026-11-05: *\"did you and your siblings forget I am disabled? why has it not\nbeen heeded lately?\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 55ka",
        "2026-11-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-05"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
